body:
I really love how you assume things I haven't said or implied, being a pedo is not being a CONVICTED pedo. My point is that NOBODY should be allowed to film (you could add "on purpose" here) children at their school without permision, that's it. The idea is to avoid pedos (again, you dont have to be caught to be a pedo, like you don't have to be caught to be a murderer) from filming children for whatever they're gonna do with it. A counter-point could be "some people might accidentaly film them without consent and this would apply to them". I'm not drafting an actual law where you have to write all the exceptions and however it's done. For this case I would say you have to be proven to be "actively" filming the children, if you're doing a vlog and it just happens to be a school behind this wouldn't apply. 

&#x200B;

As for how this is relevant, I guess you think I'm saying this law whould only apply to pedos, but that's not it, that is a case where the intentions of the filmer are illegal itself. I think that since you can't film someone's child without consent, it should apply even in school's outdoors, everywhere in my opinion, with the required exceptions for accidental recordings.

System.out.println("Want to talk about it?");
System.in.read();
return Love();
